    "    \"    plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"4feb13d4\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"`random` performs best on fairness MAD (**0.1000**), followed by `round_robin` (**0.1623**). `batch_k5` is at **0.2198**, while `advanced_local` (**0.2571**), `advanced_global` (**0.2593**), and `shortest_queue` (**0.2618**) show the largest imbalance. In the final runs, `random` and `round_robin` therefore provide the most balanced workload distribution.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"519c58f1\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Advanced Metrics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"These two metrics add a more process-level view:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **OLI** shows how much repeated offer-loop work happens per completed case.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **CHR** shows how often a case changes resource from one step to the next.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"e8015dcf\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Offer Loop Intensity (OLI) (Excluded)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Offer-related events per completed case.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"$$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\\\mathrm{OLI} = \\\\frac{\\\\#O\\\\_Create\\\\ Offer + \\\\#W\\\\_Call\\\\ after\\\\ offers + \\\\#O\\\\_Cancelled}{\\\\#\\\\text{completed cases}}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"$$\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 11,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"b3472187\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"OLI_ACTS = {\\\"O_Create Offer\\\", \\\"W_Call after offers\\\", \\\"O_Cancelled\\\"}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"oli_rows = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for method, runs in logs.items():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for run_idx, df in enumerate(runs):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        # same completed-case proxy as basic section\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        counts = df.groupby(\\\"case:concept:name\\\").size()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        completed = counts[counts > MIN_EVENTS_PER_CASE].index\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        n = len(completed)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if n == 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            continue\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        df_c = df[df[\\\"case:concept:name\\\"].isin(completed)]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        count = df_c[\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            df_c[\\\"concept:name\\\"].isin(OLI_ACTS) & (df_c[\\\"lifecycle:transition\\\"] == \\\"complete\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ].shape[0]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        oli_rows.append({\\\"method\\\": method, \\\"run\\\": run_idx, \\\"oli\\\": count / n})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"oli_df = pd.DataFrame(oli_rows)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 12,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"51f89e87\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"         method    mean    std\\n\",\n",
    "      \"         random 17.3623 0.3200\\n\",\n",
    "      \"    round_robin 17.5364 0.1425\\n\",\n",
    "      \" shortest_queue 17.1023 0.2703\\n\",\n",
    "      \"       batch_k5  4.8556 0.1168\\n\",\n",
    "      \" advanced_local 17.0634 0.2620\\n\",\n",
    "      \"advanced_global 16.3483 1.1594\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"image/png\": \"\",\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"<Figure size 990x528 with 1 Axes>\"\n",
    "      ]\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"display_data\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"oli_plot = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    oli_df.groupby(\\\"method\\\", as_index=False)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .agg(mean=(\\\"oli\\\", \\\"mean\\\"), std=(\\\"oli\\\", \\\"std\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"order = [\\\"random\\\", \\\"round_robin\\\", \\\"shortest_queue\\\", \\\"batch_k5\\\", \\\"advanced_local\\\", \\\"advanced_global\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"oli_plot[\\\"method\\\"] = pd.Categorical(oli_plot[\\\"method\\\"], categories=order, ordered=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"oli_plot = oli_plot.sort_values(\\\"method\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(oli_plot.round(4).to_string(index=False))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(9, 4.8))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.bar(oli_plot[\\\"method\\\"], oli_plot[\\\"mean\\\"], yerr=oli_plot[\\\"std\\\"], capsize=5, alpha=0.9)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel(\\\"Offer events per completed case\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xlabel(\\\"Allocation Method\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title(\\\"Offer Loop Intensity (Mean ± Std)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xticks(rotation=20, ha=\\\"right\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"bf6e4d9c\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"`batch_k5` has by far the lowest OLI at **4.8556**. All other methods are much higher: `advanced_global` **16.3483**, `advanced_local` **17.0634**, `shortest_queue` **17.1023**, `random` **17.3623**, and `round_robin` **17.5364**. Lower OLI means fewer repeated offer-loop events and therefore less repeated effort per completed case.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"45f91310\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Case Handoff Rate (CHR)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Share of consecutive case steps where the resource changes.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"$$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\\\mathrm{CHR} = \\\\frac{\\\\text{resource changes between consecutive steps}}{\\\\text{all consecutive step pairs}}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"$$\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 9,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"7992f7d4\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def case_handoff_rate(df):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # same completed-case proxy as basic section\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    counts = df.groupby(\\\"case:concept:name\\\").size()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    completed = counts[counts > MIN_EVENTS_PER_CASE].index\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if len(completed) == 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return float(\\\"nan\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df_c = df[df[\\\"case:concept:name\\\"].isin(completed)].sort_values([\\\"case:concept:name\\\", \\\"time:timestamp\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    rates = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for _, grp in df_c.groupby(\\\"case:concept:name\\\"):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        seq = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            grp[grp[\\\"lifecycle:transition\\\"] == \\\"complete\\\"][\\\"org:resource\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            .dropna()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            .tolist()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if len(seq) < 2:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            continue\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        pairs = list(zip(seq[:-1], seq[1:]))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        rates.append(sum(a != b for a, b in pairs) / len(pairs))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return float(pd.Series(rates).mean()) if rates else float(\\\"nan\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"chr_rows = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for method, runs in logs.items():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for run_idx, df in enumerate(runs):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        chr_rows.append({\\\"method\\\": method, \\\"run\\\": run_idx, \\\"chr\\\": case_handoff_rate(df)})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"chr_df = pd.DataFrame(chr_rows)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 14,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"5dff67f9\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"         method   mean    std\\n\",\n",
    "      \"         random 0.8495 0.0046\\n\",\n",
    "      \"    round_robin 0.8521 0.0054\\n\",\n",
    "      \" shortest_queue 0.4254 0.0022\\n\",\n",
    "      \"       batch_k5 0.7108 0.0050\\n\",\n",
    "      \" advanced_local 0.8427 0.0078\\n\",\n",
    "      \"advanced_global 0.8378 0.0143\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"image/png\": \"\",\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"<Figure size 990x528 with 1 Axes>\"\n",
    "      ]\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"display_data\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"chr_plot = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    chr_df.groupby(\\\"method\\\", as_index=False)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .agg(mean=(\\\"chr\\\", \\\"mean\\\"), std=(\\\"chr\\\", \\\"std\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"order = [\\\"random\\\", \\\"round_robin\\\", \\\"shortest_queue\\\", \\\"batch_k5\\\", \\\"advanced_local\\\", \\\"advanced_global\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"chr_plot[\\\"method\\\"] = pd.Categorical(chr_plot[\\\"method\\\"], categories=order, ordered=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"chr_plot = chr_plot.sort_values(\\\"method\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(chr_plot.round(4).to_string(index=False))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(9, 4.8))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.bar(chr_plot[\\\"method\\\"], chr_plot[\\\"mean\\\"], yerr=chr_plot[\\\"std\\\"], capsize=5, alpha=0.9)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel(\\\"Fraction of pairs with resource change\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xlabel(\\\"Allocation Method\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title(\\\"Case Handoff Rate (Mean ± Std)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylim(0, 1.05)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xticks(rotation=20, ha=\\\"right\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"4cfcca35\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"`shortest_queue` has the lowest CHR at **0.4254**, meaning it keeps cases with the same resource most often (more continuity). `batch_k5` is in the middle (**0.7108**). The highest handoff rates are `round_robin` (**0.8521**) and `random` (**0.8495**); `advanced_local` (**0.8427**) and `advanced_global` (**0.8378**) are slightly lower. In this metric, lower CHR reflects more continuity, while higher CHR reflects more fragmentation.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"870ea6db\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Waiting Time Ratio (proxy)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This section replaces OLI with a waiting-related **proxy** metric that is more directly linked to allocation effects.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"For a case $c$, the Waiting Time Ratio is defined as\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"$$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\\\mathrm{WTR}(c)=\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{CT}(c)-\\\\mathrm{APT}(c)}{\\\\mathrm{CT}(c)}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"$$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"where $\\\\mathrm{CT}(c)$ denotes the cycle time of case $c$ and $\\\\mathrm{APT}(c)$ denotes the sum of active processing times observed for that case. Since exact queue-entry timestamps are not logged directly, this metric should be interpreted as a waiting-related proxy rather than a direct measurement of queue waiting.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 10,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"89932255\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"         method   mean    std  total_cases  runs\\n\",\n",
    "      \"         random 0.4740 0.0101         7614     5\\n\",\n",
    "      \"    round_robin 0.4882 0.0118         7562     5\\n\",\n",
    "      \" shortest_queue 0.7292 0.0069         7659     5\\n\",\n",
    "      \"       batch_k5 0.8632 0.0043         7148     5\\n\",\n",
    "      \" advanced_local 0.7482 0.0079         7573     5\\n\",\n",
    "      \"advanced_global 0.7521 0.0345         4249     5\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"image/png\": \"\",\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"<Figure size 990x528 with 1 Axes>\"\n",
    "      ]\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"display_data\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def _pair_case_activity_intervals(df: pd.DataFrame, activities: list[str]) -> pd.DataFrame:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pair start/complete events per case/activity/resource using occurrence order.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    w = df[df[\\\"concept:name\\\"].isin(activities)].copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    w = w[w[\\\"lifecycle:transition\\\"].isin([\\\"start\\\", \\\"complete\\\"])].copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    starts = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        w[w[\\\"lifecycle:transition\\\"] == \\\"start\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        [[\\\"case:concept:name\\\", \\\"concept:name\\\", \\\"org:resource\\\", \\\"time:timestamp\\\"]]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .sort_values([\\\"case:concept:name\\\", \\\"concept:name\\\", \\\"org:resource\\\", \\\"time:timestamp\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    starts[\\\"idx\\\"] = starts.groupby([\\\"case:concept:name\\\", \\\"concept:name\\\", \\\"org:resource\\\"]).cumcount()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    starts = starts.rename(columns={\\\"time:timestamp\\\": \\\"start_time\\\"})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    completes = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        w[w[\\\"lifecycle:transition\\\"] == \\\"complete\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        [[\\\"case:concept:name\\\", \\\"concept:name\\\", \\\"org:resource\\\", \\\"time:timestamp\\\"]]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .sort_values([\\\"case:concept:name\\\", \\\"concept:name\\\", \\\"org:resource\\\", \\\"time:timestamp\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    completes[\\\"idx\\\"] = completes.groupby([\\\"case:concept:name\\\", \\\"concept:name\\\", \\\"org:resource\\\"]).cumcount()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    completes = completes.rename(columns={\\\"time:timestamp\\\": \\\"end_time\\\"})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    merged = pd.merge(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        starts,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        completes,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        on=[\\\"case:concept:name\\\", \\\"concept:name\\\", \\\"org:resource\\\", \\\"idx\\\"],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        how=\\\"inner\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    merged[\\\"active_seconds\\\"] = (merged[\\\"end_time\\\"] - merged[\\\"start_time\\\"]).dt.total_seconds().clip(lower=0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return merged\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def compute_nptr_case_level(df: pd.DataFrame, min_events_per_case: int = 2) -> pd.Series:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Compute NPTR per completed case from existing event-log CSV data.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    counts = df.groupby(\\\"case:concept:name\\\").size()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    completed = counts[counts > min_events_per_case].index\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df_c = df[df[\\\"case:concept:name\\\"].isin(completed)].copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if df_c.empty:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return pd.Series(dtype=float, name=\\\"nptr\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cycle = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        df_c.groupby(\\\"case:concept:name\\\")[\\\"time:timestamp\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .agg([\\\"min\\\", \\\"max\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cycle_seconds = (cycle[\\\"max\\\"] - cycle[\\\"min\\\"]).dt.total_seconds().clip(lower=0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    intervals = _pair_case_activity_intervals(df_c, W_ACTIVITIES)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if intervals.empty:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        active_by_case = pd.Series(0.0, index=cycle_seconds.index)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        active_by_case = intervals.groupby(\\\"case:concept:name\\\")[\\\"active_seconds\\\"].sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        active_by_case = active_by_case.reindex(cycle_seconds.index, fill_value=0.0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    denom = cycle_seconds.where(cycle_seconds > 0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    nptr = ((cycle_seconds - active_by_case) / denom).clip(lower=0, upper=1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    nptr = nptr.dropna()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    nptr.name = \\\"nptr\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return nptr\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"nptr_rows = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for method, runs in logs.items():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for run_idx, df in enumerate(runs):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        nptr_case = compute_nptr_case_level(df, min_events_per_case=MIN_EVENTS_PER_CASE)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if nptr_case.empty:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            continue\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        nptr_rows.append({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"method\\\": method,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"run\\\": run_idx,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"n_cases\\\": int(nptr_case.shape[0]),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"nptr_mean\\\": float(nptr_case.mean()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"nptr_std_cases\\\": float(nptr_case.std(ddof=0)),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"nptr_df = pd.DataFrame(nptr_rows)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if nptr_df.empty:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"No NPTR results available. Check loaded logs in data/<method>/.\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    nptr_plot = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        nptr_df.groupby(\\\"method\\\", as_index=False)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .agg(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            mean=(\\\"nptr_mean\\\", \\\"mean\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            std=(\\\"nptr_mean\\\", \\\"std\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            total_cases=(\\\"n_cases\\\", \\\"sum\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            runs=(\\\"run\\\", \\\"count\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    order = [\\\"random\\\", \\\"round_robin\\\", \\\"shortest_queue\\\", \\\"batch_k5\\\", \\\"advanced_local\\\", \\\"advanced_global\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    nptr_plot[\\\"method\\\"] = pd.Categorical(nptr_plot[\\\"method\\\"], categories=order, ordered=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    nptr_plot = nptr_plot.sort_values(\\\"method\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(nptr_plot.round(4).to_string(index=False))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.figure(figsize=(9, 4.8))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.bar(nptr_plot[\\\"method\\\"], nptr_plot[\\\"mean\\\"], yerr=nptr_plot[\\\"std\\\"], capsize=5, alpha=0.9)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.ylabel(\\\"Share of case duration outside active processing\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.xlabel(\\\"Allocation Method\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.title(\\\"Non-Processing Time Ratio (NPTR, Mean ± Std Across Runs)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.ylim(0, 1.05)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.xticks(rotation=20, ha=\\\"right\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"541664f5\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"The Waiting Time Ratio (proxy) should be interpreted as follows:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Lower WTR**: a larger fraction of case duration is spent in active processing—indicating efficient allocation with less idle/non-processing time.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Higher WTR**: more elapsed time occurs outside active processing (e.g., waiting for resources, routing delays, or other non-active intervals)—indicating potential allocation bottlenecks.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Caveat: The remainder (cycle time minus active processing time) may include routing delays, modeled non-processing delays, or other inactive time between activities, not exclusively queue waiting. Thus WTR is a waiting-related proxy, defensible when framed as the share of total case duration not spent in active processing intervals, not as a direct measure of observed queue waiting.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This makes WTR more allocation-relevant and more defensible than OLI under a fixed simulation horizon, while keeping CHR as the continuity metric.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"055cc19b\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Pareto Trade-off (Cycle Time vs Fairness MAD)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This plot highlights the core trade-off between speed and workload balance.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- x-axis: mean cycle time (hours), lower is better\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- y-axis: mean fairness MAD, lower is better\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- points on the Pareto frontier are non-dominated\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
